    "body": "In this episode of The Pentagon Buzz, Breaking Defense’s Ashley Roque breaks down two major Pentagon initiatives after a recent conversation with Dale Marks , who is responsible for installations and energy at the Defense Department.\nFirst, the Pentagon is soliciting proposals from governors for a new stateside base , with a decision expected by June 2027. Then, Ashley talks about how the Pentagon’s FORTRESS America initiative is intended to strengthen current installations against a wide range of threats, possibly with help from private industry.\nSubscribe to our Pentagon newsletter to get the latest information from the building delivered directly to you.\nBreaking Defense Video\nThe Pentagon wants a massive new military base. Where will it go?\nWatch Now »\nWhat now? Budget fight, Hegseth impeachment on deck for defense-focused lawmakers after midterms\nWatch Now »\nThe defense show circuit keeps rolling, plus Jimmy Stewart goes to war\nWatch Now »\nQatar’s domestic weapons, Turkey’s drone arsenal and the Mecca pact’s next test\nWatch Now »\n3 congressional races that matter for defense\nWatch Now »\nHow General Atomics views Europe’s unmanned future\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nA more flexible way to defend maneuver forces from drones that doesn’t tie them down [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nWhat’s haunting the Pentagon this Halloween?\nWatch Now »\npresented by\nThe new must-have capabilities for drones [Sponsored]\nWatch Now »\nArmy’s tech chief talks autonomy, acquisition and the future of drones\nWatch Now »\nScroll for more video",
